// The field camera (k_fldCamera.c) and its neighbours in the band 0x1D5220-0x1D75E8 (game/include/p3fes/game/
// field3_camera.h), from SLUS_216.21. Phase 5 slice `field3`, part `camera`: generated by p3fes_handgen (one statement
// per instruction on the hg_cpu register view: frame, spills, $ra links, cycle charges and check points exactly as the
// recompiled bodies) and made readable on top -- block roles, named offsets, comments; no statement moved.
// tests/game/test_field3_camera.cpp pairs each body with its __recomp body on random worlds, on the stand-in world
// (tests/game/stand_ins.h) and on the Tartarus replay snapshot climb_ref_17000.
//
// The field camera controller (docs/ANALYSIS/26_field.md section 4.4): a "field camera controler" kwln task (priority
// 10, sField+4) whose 208-byte work owns a PIVOT RwFrame inserted between the main camera's frame and that frame's
// parent. Each frame the pivot follows the target resource (+204; its collision controller +480 gives the position)
// plus an offset, inside a dead-zone cylinder: it moves horizontally only by what exceeds the radius (+32) and
// vertically only by what exceeds half the height (+36). Modes (+8): 0 / 5 the main camera's frame hangs under the
// pivot (it rides along); 2 the main camera's frame hangs under the original parent and is re-aimed at the pivot
// (sub_1A1210) whenever the pivot moved; 3 the rail camera (the pivot runs along the field's camera spline, the
// collision record's +2588, sampled at nine points t = i / 8 into +96; debug printf); 4 the rail points only; 1 none.
// The debug cylinder (sub_1A4860, the task's first child) shows the dead zone when flag bit 31 is set.
//
// Also here: the camera's rotation tasks ("field camera rotation": turn the main camera about the world y axis over N
// frames on a sine ease, to the hero's facing quadrant or a given angle), the camera save / restore used around
// battles (a 96-byte record), the per-field camera set-up from the .CMR file, the field pack or the scene's camera
// resource (type 20), the opmap table loader, and the shadow encounter picker sub_1D7300 (k_encount data: it only
// sits in this band).
//
// RW callees (names from game/src/render/core3.cpp where read there, otherwise inferred from their use here):
// sub_4CAF10 create a frame, sub_4CAF80 destroy it, sub_4CB930 reset it, sub_4CB420 (parent, child) add a child,
// sub_4CB590 (frame) remove from its parent, sub_4CB750 (frame, v, 2) translate (post-concatenated),
// sub_4CB890 (frame, axis, $f12 angle, 2) rotate, sub_4CB7F0 [RwFrameTransform] (frame, matrix, 0), sub_4CB2F0
// [RwFrameGetLTM], sub_4C69F0 normalise a vector, sub_4C2FB0 a matrix copy; RwCalloc / RwFree / RwMalloc through the
// slots 0x960184 / 0x96017C. Main camera (sub_198590, draw_layer): object +4 its RwFrame; frame +4 parent, +16 the
// modelling matrix, +64 its position row. sub_1A1210(camera, eye, target, 0) aims the main camera; sub_1A4580 /
// sub_1A4600 set / get its field of view ($f12 / $f0).
#include "p3fes/game/hg_cpu.h"
#include "p3fes/game/field3_camera.h"

